-- Betadine Ointment (povidone-iodine)
insert into public.medicine_details (medicine_id, medicine_activity, uses, side_effects, composition, manufacturer_details, generation_status, generated_at)
values (15, 'Bupivacaine blocks the generation and the conduction of nerve impulses, presumably by increasing the threshold for electrical excitation in the nerve, by slowing the propagation of the nerve impulse, and by reducing the rate of rise of the action potential. In general, the progression of anesthesia is related to the diameter, myelination, and conduction velocity of affected nerve fibers. Clinically, the order of loss of nerve function is as follows: (1) pain, (2) temperature, (3) touch, (4) proprioception, and (5) skeletal muscle tone.', 'First aid to help prevent infection in minor cuts scrapes burns', 'The following clinically significant adverse reactions have been reported and described in the Warnings and Precautions section of the labeling: Cardiac Arrest in Obstetrical Anesthesia [see Warnings and Precautions (5.1) ] Dose-Related Toxicity [see Warnings and Precautions (5.2) ] Methemoglobinemia [see Warnings and Precautions (5.3) ] Chondrolysis with Intra-Articular Infusion [see Warnings and Precautions (5.5) ] Cardiac Arrest with Intravenous Regional Anesthesia Use [see Contraindications (4) , Warnings and Precautions (5.7) ] Systemic Toxicities with Unintended Intra…', 'Active ingredient: Povidone-iodine. Marketed as: Povidone-iodine antiseptic ointment for wound care and infection prevention. Ingredient names normalised against RxNorm (RxCUI 8611).', 'Marketed in India by Win-Medicare. Reference label filed by Atlantis Consumer Healthcare, Inc. (openFDA).', 'generated', now())
