-- Ciplox 500 (ciprofloxacin)
insert into public.medicine_details (medicine_id, medicine_activity, uses, side_effects, composition, manufacturer_details, generation_status, generated_at)
values (43, 'Ciprofloxacin is a member of the fluoroquinolone class of antibacterial agents [see Microbiology (12.4) ] .', 'Ciprofloxacin Ophthalmic Solution is indicated for the treatment of infections caused by susceptible strains of the designated microorganisms in the conditions listed below: Corneal Ulcers: Pseudomonas aeruginosa Serratia marcescens * Staphylococcus aureus Staphylococcus epidermidis Streptococcus pneumoniae Streptococcus (Viridans Group) * Conjunctivitis: Haemophilus influenzae Staphylococcus aureus Staphylococcus epidermidis Streptococcus pneumoniae *Efficacy for this organism was studied in fewer than 10 infections.', 'The most frequently reported drug related adverse reaction was local burning or discomfort. In corneal ulcer studies with frequent administration of the drug, white crystalline precipitates were seen in approximately 17% of patients ( see Precautions ). Other reactions occurring in less than 10% of patients included lid margin crusting, crystals/scales, foreign body sensation, itching, conjunctival hyperemia and a bad taste following instillation.', 'Active ingredient: Ciprofloxacin. Marketed as: Ciprofloxacin antibiotic tablet for bacterial infections. Ingredient names normalised against RxNorm (RxCUI 2551).', 'Marketed in India by Cipla. Reference label filed by Proficient Rx LP (openFDA).', 'generated', now())
