-- Deriphyllin Retard (theophylline)
insert into public.medicine_details (medicine_id, medicine_activity, uses, side_effects, composition, manufacturer_details, generation_status, generated_at)
values (74, 'Theophylline has two distinct actions in the airways of patients with reversible obstruction; smooth muscle relaxation (i.e., bronchodilation) and suppression of the response of the airways to stimuli (i.e., non-bronchodilator prophylactic effects).', 'Theophylline is indicated for the treatment of the symptoms and reversible airflow obstruction associated with chronic asthma and other chronic lung diseases, e.g., emphysema and chronic bronchitis.', 'associated with theophylline are generally mild when peak serum theophylline concentrations are <20 mcg/mL and mainly consist of transient caffeine-like adverse effects such as nausea, vomiting, headache and insomnia. When peak serum theophylline concentrations exceed 20 mcg/mL, however, theophylline produces a wide range of adverse reactions including persistent vomiting, cardiac arrhythmias, and intractable seizures which can be lethal (see OVERDOSAGE ).', 'Active ingredient: Theophylline. Marketed as: Theophylline-based tablet for management of asthma and bronchitis. Ingredient names normalised against RxNorm (RxCUI 10438).', 'Marketed in India by Zuventus Healthcare. Reference label filed by Westminster Pharmaceuticals, LLC (openFDA).', 'generated', now())
